    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-29885",
      "knowledge_point_id": "3c865ec2-5bed-5892-966b-a586097be923",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating the Sum of a Reciprocal Function and a Power Function",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\int ({x}^{2/3}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{x})\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we apply the sum rule and get\n\n$$\n\\int ({x}^{2/3}+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{x})\\,\\text{d}x=\\int {x}^{2/3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\sqrt{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nNow, using the power rule in the first term, and taking out the coefficient in the second term, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2/3}\\,\\text{d}x+\\sqrt{2}\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{2/3+1}}{\\frac{2}{3}+1}+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{5}{x}^{5/3}+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{7}{5}{x}^{4/3}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{3\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{5}{x}^{5/3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{11}{5}{x}^{11/3}+\\sqrt{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{9}{5}{x}^{7/3}+\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{3}{5}{x}^{5/3}+\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C",
              "option": "4",
