  {
    "directory": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13943118",
    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-103546",
      "knowledge_point_id": "55a323ba-f2a7-5a49-abd4-a9812518ef8c",
      "knowledge_point": "Determining the Equation of a Normal Line to a Curve at a Point",
      "problem": "The equation of the normal line to the curve $y=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}$ at the point $(1,4)$ is given by $x+py=q$ where $p$ and $q$ are constants. Find the value of $q-p.$",
      "worked_solution": "Let $f(x)=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}.$ First, we compute the derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4{x}^{-1/2}) \\\\  & =-2{x}^{-3/2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{x}^{3}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the slope of the tangent at the point $(1,4):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m={f}^{′}(1)=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{{1}^{3}}}=-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope of the normal line ${m}^{′}$ is\n\n$$\n{m}^{′}=-\\frac{1}{m}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, the equation of the normal line is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-4 & =\\frac{1}{2}(x-1) \\\\ 2y-8 & =x-1 \\\\ x-2y & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $q-p=-7-(-2)=-5.$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-4",
              "option": "0",
              "source_option": "a"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-1",
              "option": "1",
              "source_option": "b"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "8",
              "option": "2",
              "source_option": "c"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-5",
              "option": "3",
              "source_option": "d"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "3",
              "option": "4",
              "source_option": "e"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "knowledge_point_source_id": 6080,
